From 5dc295d36d8b0fee7efc2fcd389ca64727883804 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:43:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] Drop the two dead buttons under Telegram alerts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Message seller" linked to /items/{id}/want_it/new and "Buy" to
/transaction/buy/new?transaction[item_id]=…, the deep links every Vinted
notifier on GitHub has copied from one another since 2022. Vinted's front
end was rebuilt and both answer "page not found"; checkout now needs a
transaction the site creates when you press "Buy now", so there is no
address that opens it. The listing page carries both actions right under
the price, so the alert now offers "Open listing" and "Seller profile"
(/member/{id}, which does resolve). urls.message_seller_url and buy_url
return the listing page so the webhook's version-1 `links` keys keep
working; `links.seller` is added.
---
